# Goteverse — Base Rules

Goteverse is a USD-based digital twin of a stadium and surrounding city, streamed from NVIDIA Omniverse Kit (Python) to a React/TypeScript web frontend via WebRTC. The two sides communicate over a WebRTC data channel. Implement features **web-side** when possible; new backend features go in modular Kit extensions wired to existing services. Composer is for world building; the viewer is for runtime.

**Rule hierarchy**: This file (always-applied) → `topic-index.mdc` (domain-grouped reference) → `.cursor/rules/topics/*.mdc` (deep-dive per feature). Before starting work on a new feature area, read `topic-index.mdc` to identify which topic files are relevant, then read those topic files — that split exists so agents do **not** need every topic file for every task.

